The  PI 4 then controls the vehicle movement through a motor driver (L298N/L293D) connected to DC motors.
When the vehicle is positioned over the weed, the PI 4 activates the laser module using a relay or transistor circuit. 
The laser emits high-intensity heat to destroy the weed stem without using chemical herbicides. 
After a preset time, the laser is turned off and the PI 4 commands the motors to move the vehicle forward. 
This process repeats continuously for autonomous and precise weed control.
